GIMP Palette
Name: Rhythm — Vaporwave Lanes
Columns: 4
#
# Direction: a chrome grid running to a synthetic horizon. Everything emits
# light; nothing reflects it.
#
# A rhythm game is judged in tens of milliseconds, so the palette is built
# around timing rather than mood. neon-aqua-* is the approach colour and
# neon-pink-* is the strike colour, and they are near-complementary so the
# instant a note crosses the judgement line the change is the largest one the
# screen can make. The player reacts to that flip before reading anything.
#
# grid-dim and grid-lit are one pair, not a ramp: the lane floor is either on
# the beat or it is not, and an in-between step would blur the only cue that
# tells the player where the beat actually is.
#
 26  26  26	outline
 16  10  32	night-0
 34  20  60	night-1
 58  32  96	night-2
 88  50 140	night-3-rim
232  56 148	neon-pink-0
255 108 186	neon-pink-1
255 176 222	neon-pink-2-glow
 40 200 208	neon-aqua-0
110 236 240	neon-aqua-1
196 252 254	neon-aqua-2-glow
250 176  64	sun-0
254 214 118	sun-1
255 244 196	sun-2-glow
 92  96 124	grid-dim
148 152 184	grid-lit
255 255 255	spark
